  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to read this view",
      "items": [
        "Each row is an independent guarded transition, not a chronological sequence across rows. Repeated phase labels name the same underlying phase; aliases prevent unrelated rules from sharing ambiguous drawing corridors. The normal-procedure view supplies the connected happy path."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Human-only enrolment",
      "items": [
        "Mission Lua lists only units from coalition.getPlayers that have a non-empty player name and are airplanes or helicopters. The Python side drops any entry without human: true (overlord_carrier.lua 500-508, carrier.py 204-215).",
        "AI and unregistered aircraft are never polled. Only units on the brain's watch list are sampled, and the list expires after the lease, 15 s by default (overlord_carrier.lua 26-32, 81, 621-626).",
        "An SRS radio name that does not uniquely identify the spoken caller is refused (sender_identifies; airfield.py 1428-1433, carrier.py 1025-1030)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Incarnations and epochs",
      "items": [
        "Incarnation = unit id plus a serial. The serial advances on birth or on any player, unit-name, coalition or terminal change, and is never reset within the scripting state (overlord_carrier.lua 26-28, 514-521; overlord_airfield.lua 83).",
        "The hook makes a new epoch at every simulation start. The services retire old epochs and reject stale seq. The brain fences retired epochs across both native roles (overlord_hook.lua 661-669, brain.py 75-91)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Replies re-validated before transmit",
      "items": [
        "state: needs a fresh bridge and the same session revision.",
        "notice: needs the same radio and epoch, and the same occupant (incarnation + generation) when addressed.",
        "facts (airfield only): needs a fresh bridge and the exact spoken facts (airfield.py 1242-1281, carrier.py 904-937).",
        "Queued notifications expire after 10 s, replies after 15 s. The Gateway re-checks _bound and /validate-event just before TX (gateway.py 256-273)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Transition evidence (file lines)",
      "items": [
        "heard \u2192 identified (one human catalog match): coalition-filtered; ambiguity refused (identities.py 7-28)",
        "identified \u2192 enrolled (enrolling intent): airfield startup/taxi/inbound/emergency; carrier checkIn/departure/emergency",
        "enrolled \u2192 watched (next accepted exchange): issued_seq set, watch returned (624-630)",
        "watched \u2192 closed (lifecycle event, absence, bad sample, or incarnation change): dead/eject/disconnect/birth, absent > 1 snapshot, invalid sample",
        "heard \u2192 ignored (not addressed: no reply): parse None or other field's name: reply None",
        "identified \u2192 ignored (no enrolment: notice only): notice only: 'check in first' / 'no active session'",
        "watched \u2192 suspended (bridge stale): stale_seconds without snapshot",
        "suspended \u2192 watched (fresh snapshot): watch re-handshake (622-629, 480-488)",
        "watched \u2192 transferred (enrols in other family): brain releases prior family (brain.py 172-180)",
        "watched \u2192 epoch_reset (new mission epoch): service reset; retired epoch refused",
        "watched \u2192 closed, incarnation or coalition change: respawn, slot or coalition change (airfield.py 714-718, carrier.py 548-552)"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
